 "briefing": "# Razorpay Briefing: 16 October to 15 November 2026\n\n**Meeting date:** 17 November 2026\n**Research window:** 16 October 2026 to 15 November 2026\n\n## Research Status\n\nNo changes at Razorpay in the research window could be verified. Every search attempt returned no results, so no news items, product launches, leadership changes, or deals were confirmed. No facts are cited in this briefing, and no dates are flagged as unverified because no candidate items were found.\n\nThe absence of results reflects a failure of the search tool, not evidence that Razorpay was inactive. Razorpay's own pages and the press were not reached, so this briefing should not be read as confirmation that nothing changed.\n\n## Category Summary\n\n- **News:** No change verified. Razorpay's newsroom and blog were not reached [1].\n- **Product or feature launches:** No change verified. The changelog and product update pages were not reached [1].\n- **Hires and leadership changes:** No change verified. Leadership pages and the company's LinkedIn page were not reached [1][2].\n- **Deals, partnerships, funding, or acquisitions:** No change verified. Filings and press coverage were not reached [3][4].\n\n## Checks to Complete Before 17 November\n\nThese checks should be completed manually and filtered to 16 October to 15 November 2026:\n\n1. **Razorpay newsroom, press, and blog** on the official website [1].\n2. **Razorpay changelog, release notes, and product updates** on the official website [1].\n3. **Razorpay leadership and about pages**, plus the company's LinkedIn page and the LinkedIn profiles of any named executives [2].\n4. **Indian business and tech press**, searched for \"Razorpay\" with a date filter: Entrackr [5], Inc42 [6], Economic Times [7], Moneycontrol [8], and Mint [9].\n5. **International tech and business press**, using the same filter: TechCrunch [10] and Reuters [11].\n6. **Ministry of Corporate Affairs filings** for share allotments, share transfers, and acquisitions [3].\n\nAny item found through these checks should be confirmed against its primary source and dated before it is used in the meeting.\n\n## Open Questions for the Meeting\n\n1. Which product, feature, or API changes did Razorpay publish between 16 October and 15 November 2026, and where are they documented, such as in a changelog, release notes, or the blog?\n2. Has the leadership team or board changed in this window, and if so, were those changes announced on Razorpay's website or LinkedIn?\n3. Has Razorpay announced or completed any funding, secondary share sale, partnership, or acquisition in this window, and which of those items are public?\n\n### Sources\n\n[1] Razorpay official website: https://razorpay.com\n[2] Razorpay on LinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/company/razorpay\n[3] Ministry of Corporate Affairs (MCA21) portal: https://www.mca.gov.in\n[4] Razorpay Economic Times coverage (search destination): https://economictimes.indiatimes.com\n[5] Entrackr (search destination): https://entrackr.com\n[6] Inc42 (search destination): https://inc42.com\n[7] The Economic Times (search destination): https://economictimes.indiatimes.com\n[8] Moneycontrol (search destination): https://www.moneycontrol.com\n[9] Mint (search destination): https://www.livemint.com\n[10] TechCrunch (search destination): https://techcrunch.com\n[11] Reuters (search destination): https://www.reuters.com",
